   "id": 532675,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the surface area of the triangular prism shown.<br>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/dba1ee3d3d9163db.png\" alt=\"A triangular prism. The sides of the triangle are labeled l equals 7 centimeters, w equals 6 centimeters, and w equals 5 centimeters. The height of the triangle is labeled h equals 4 centimeters. The height of the prism is labeled h equals 4 centimeters.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The surface area of a right prism where <i>B</i> is the area of the base, <i>p</i> is the perimeter of the base, and <i>h</i> is the height is <span data-math=\"SA = 2B + ph\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The area of the triangular base is <span data-math=\"A = \\frac{1}{2}bh\"></span>, where <i>b</i> represents the base and <i>h</i> represents the height.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = \\frac{1}{2}bh = \\frac{1}{2}\\left( {{\\text{7 cm}}} \\right)\\left( {{\\text{4 cm}}} \\right) = {\\text{ 14 c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}\"></span></p>\n<p>The perimeter of the base <span data-math=\"= p = {\\text{ }}6{\\text{ cm }} + {\\text{ }}7{\\text{ cm }} + {\\text{ }}5{\\text{ cm }} = {\\text{ }}18{\\text{ cm}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The surface area <span data-math=\"= {\\text{ }}2B + ph = {\\text{ }}2\\left( {14{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}} \\right){\\text{ }} + {\\text{ }}\\left( {18{\\text{ cm}}} \\right)\\left( {4{\\text{ cm}}} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}28{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2} + {\\text{ }}72{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2} = {\\text{ }}100{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The surface area is 100 square centimeters.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"100\\,\\text{cm}{^2}\">100\\,\\text{cm}{^2}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
